<title>NORWAY: SKI JUMPING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SKI JUMPING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LILLEHAMMER, Norway 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in a</p>
<p>World Cup high hill (120-metre) ski jumping event on Sunday:</p>
<p> 1. Kristian Brenden  (Norway)     267.6 points  (first jump</p>
<p>127.0/second jump 130.0)</p>
<p> 2. Espen Bredesen  (Norway)	 267.2  (121.5/135.0)</p>
<p> 3. Dieter Thoma  (Germany)	  261.8  (126.0/132.5)</p>
<p>4. Andreas Goldberger  (Austria)  256.7  (121.5/132.5)</p>
<p> 5. Kazuyoshi Funaki  (Japan)	253.2  (123.5/125.5)</p>
<p> 6. Roar Ljoekelsoey  (Norway)     249.0  (127.0/120.5)</p>
<p> 7. Kent Johanssen  (Norway)	 247.5  (122.5/125.0)</p>
<p> 7. Nicolas Dessum  (France)	 247.5  (121.0/126.5)</p>
<p> 9. Hiroya Saitoh  (Japan)	   246.7  (121.0/125.5)</p>
<p> 10. Primoz Peterka  (Slovakia)    242.7  (118.0/128.5)</p>
<p>Leading World Cup standings (after two events):</p>
<p> 1. Brenden			180 points</p>
<p> 2. Thoma			  160</p>
<p> 3. Bredesen		     106</p>
<p> 4. Gold berger		   90</p>
<p> 5. Saitoh			  89</p>
<p> 6. Peterka			 76</p>
